Subject: [flux] A new tab is the console

The console is the product's home screen, so it replaces the new tab page
rather than being one more thing to navigate to. NewTabURLDetails::ForProfile
is the single place that decides what chrome://newtab resolves to - the
rewrite, the omnibox's reverse rewrite and the instant-process checks all read
from it - so returning early here covers every path that opens a tab.

Off-the-record profiles keep Chromium's incognito NTP: the console is signed
into the user's connectors and has no business being the landing page of a
window whose point is that it remembers nothing.

--- a/chrome/browser/search/search.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/search/search.cc
@@ -164,6 +164,16 @@
       : url(url), state(state) {}
 
   static NewTabURLDetails ForProfile(Profile* profile) {
+    // In Flux a new tab is the console. It is the product's home screen rather
+    // than a search page, so it replaces the NTP outright instead of competing
+    // with the default search provider's - which is also why this returns
+    // before the DefaultSearchProviderIsGoogle() branch below rather than
+    // being wired in as one more candidate.
+    if (profile && !profile->IsOffTheRecord()) {
+      return NewTabURLDetails(GURL(chrome::kChromeUIFluxURL),
+                              NEW_TAB_URL_VALID);
+    }
+
     // Incognito and Guest profiles have their own New Tab.
     // This function may also be called by other off-the-record profiles that
     // can exceptionally open a browser window.
